.TH SETPRIORITY 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
setpriority \- sets the nice value for matching processes, subject to resource limits and privileges
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/resource.h>
.B int setpriority(int which, unsigned int who, int priority);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets the nice value for matching processes, subject to resource limits and privileges.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setpriority (2)
